{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_018EZjz2TEXeMJdAELdDcSEk","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Plan: Ping-Pong MLE Fold Buffers\n2\t\n3\t## Goal\n4\t\n5\tEliminate ~67K per-benchmark DeviceMatrix allocations and ~67K frees in the constraints-phase MLE fold (`fold_mle_evals`) by replacing them with two pre-allocated contiguous device buffers used in a ping-pong pattern. MLE Rounds at APC 300 take 173ms, of which ~15-20ms is CUDA memory pool API overhead from these allocations (confirmed by the bulk-alloc-mle-fold-buffers task which recovered 13ms with a heavier ArenaMatrix approach). This cleaner implementation avoids the ArenaMatrix/MatrixRef/FoldArena type complexity of the previous attempt.\n6\t\n7\t## Current Code Path\n8\t\n9\t### MLE Rounds loop\n10\t`crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/mod.rs:631-648`\n11\t```rust\n12\tfor round in 1..=n_max {\n13\t    let sp_round_evals = prover.sumcheck_polys_batch_eval(round, r[round - 1])?;\n14\t    // ... transcript observe, sample r_round ...\n15\t    prover.fold_mle_evals(round, r_round)?;\n16\t}\n17\t```\n18\t\n19\t### fold_mle_evals\n20\t`crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/mod.rs:1999-2091`\n21\t\n22\tContains `batch_fold` closure (lines 2002-2048):\n23\t1. Counts foldable matrices (height > 1) via `partition_point` (line 2003)\n24\t2. Allocates output: `DeviceMatrix::<EF>::with_capacity(output_height, width)` per foldable matrix (line 2014) → `cudaMallocAsync`\n25\t3. Collects input/output pointer Vecs (lines 2019-2027)\n26\t4. Uploads 4 pointer arrays to device (lines 2029-2032)\n27\t5. Launches single `batch_fold_mle` kernel (lines 2034-2044)\n28\t6. Returns new output matrices, dropping old inputs → `cudaFreeAsync` each\n29\t\n30\tCalled twice per round:\n31\t- `mat_evals_per_trace` (lines 2050-2066): ~800 matrices at APC 300\n32\t- `sels_per_trace` (line 2078): ~623 matrices\n33\t\n34\tPer round: ~1400 allocs + ~1400 frees = ~2800 CUDA API calls.\n35\tPer benchmark (24 rounds × 2 segments): ~134K API calls (~67K allocs, ~67K frees).\n36\tAt 0.3-0.5μs per call: **20-33ms total overhead** (previous task confirmed 13ms recovery, suggesting ~15-20ms was actual overhead).\n37\t\n38\t### sumcheck_polys_batch_eval\n39\t`crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/mod.rs:1536-1922`\n40\t\n41\tReads `self.mat_evals_per_trace[trace_idx][mat_idx]` and `self.sels_per_trace[trace_idx]` to get `.buffer().as_ptr()`, `.height()`, `.width()`. These are the DeviceMatrix objects being replaced.\n42\t\n43\t### into_column_openings\n44\t`crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/mod.rs:2098+`\n45\t\n46\tCalls `m.to_host()` on each final DeviceMatrix to get column openings. Must still work after replacement.\n47\t\n48\t## Changes\n49\t\n50\t### 1. Add ping-pong buffer state to LogupZerocheckGpu\n51\t\n52\t**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/mod.rs`\n53\t\n54\tAdd fields to `LogupZerocheckGpu`:\n55\t```rust\n56\t/// Ping-pong buffer A for mat_evals fold (current round's data)\n57\tmat_fold_buf_a: DeviceBuffer<EF>,\n58\t/// Ping-pong buffer B for mat_evals fold (next round's output)\n59\tmat_fold_buf_b: DeviceBuffer<EF>,\n60\t/// Per-matrix (height, width) — updated each fold (height halves)\n61\tmat_fold_sizes: Vec<(usize, usize)>,\n62\t/// Per-matrix byte offset within the current buffer\n63\tmat_fold_offsets: Vec<usize>,\n64\t/// Per-trace count of matrices (to reconstruct nested structure)\n65\tmat_per_trace_counts: Vec<usize>,\n66\t/// Same for sels\n67\tsel_fold_buf_a: DeviceBuffer<EF>,\n68\tsel_fold_buf_b: DeviceBuffer<EF>,\n69\tsel_fold_sizes: Vec<(usize, usize)>,\n70\tsel_fold_offsets: Vec<usize>,\n71\t```\n72\t\n73\t### 2. Initialize ping-pong buffers before MLE loop\n74\t\n75\t**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/mod.rs`\n76\t\n77\tAfter `fold_ple_evals` (line 617) and before the MLE loop (line 631), compute layout metadata and allocate buffer B only (buffer A is the original DeviceMatrix data, used in round 1):\n78\t\n79\t```rust\n80\t// Compute per-matrix metadata for ping-pong layout.\n81\tstruct MatSlice { offset: usize, height: usize, width: usize }\n82\t\n83\tlet mat_slices: Vec<MatSlice> = self.mat_evals_per_trace.iter()\n84\t    .flatten()\n85\t    .map(|m| MatSlice { offset: 0 /* filled after round 1 */, height: m.height(), width: m.width() })\n86\t    .collect();\n87\tlet mat_per_trace_counts: Vec<usize> = self.mat_evals_per_trace.iter()\n88\t    .map(|v| v.len()).collect();\n89\t// Prefix sums for per-trace indexing into flat array\n90\tlet mat_per_trace_prefix: Vec<usize> = mat_per_trace_counts.iter()\n91\t    .scan(0, |acc, &c| { let v = *acc; *acc += c; Some(v) }).collect();\n92\tlet mat_total: usize = mat_slices.iter().map(|s| s.height * s.width).sum();\n93\t\n94\tlet sel_slices: Vec<MatSlice> = self.sels_per_trace.iter()\n95\t    .map(|m| MatSlice { offset: 0, height: m.height(), width: m.width() }).collect();\n96\tlet sel_total: usize = sel_slices.iter().map(|s| s.height * s.width).sum();\n97\t\n98\t// Allocate ONE ping-pong buffer (B). Round 1 reads from original DeviceMatrix data,\n99\t// writes into buffer B. Then drop originals and allocate buffer A for round 2 output.\n100\tlet mut mat_buf_b = DeviceBuffer::<EF>::with_capacity(mat_total);\n101\tlet mut sel_buf_b = DeviceBuffer::<EF>::with_capacity(sel_total);\n102\t```\n103\t\n104\t**D2D copy primitive**: For all D2D copies throughout this plan, use the existing `cuda_memcpy::<true, true>(dst as *mut c_void, src as *const c_void, count * size_of::<EF>())` from `crates/cuda-common/src/copy.rs:42`. No new helper function needed.\n105\t\n106\tPack mat_evals and sels into their respective buffer A via D2D copies:\n107\t\n108\t```rust\n109\tlet mut mat_offsets = Vec::with_capacity(mat_slices.len());\n110\tlet mut off = 0usize;\n111\tfor m in self.mat_evals_per_trace.iter().flatten() {\n112\t    let bytes = m.buffer().len() * std::mem::size_of::<EF>();\n113\t    unsafe { cuda_memcpy::<true, true>(\n114\t        mat_buf_a.as_mut_ptr().add(off) as *mut c_void,\n115\t        m.buffer().as_ptr() as *const c_void, bytes); }\n116\t    mat_offsets.push(off);\n117\t    off += m.buffer().len();\n118\t}\n119\t// Update mat_slices with computed offsets\n120\tfor (s, &o) in mat_slices.iter_mut().zip(&mat_offsets) { s.offset = o; }\n121\t\n122\t// Same for sels into sel_buf_a\n123\tlet mut sel_offsets = Vec::with_capacity(sel_slices.len());\n124\toff = 0;\n125\tfor m in &self.sels_per_trace {\n126\t    let bytes = m.buffer().len() * std::mem::size_of::<EF>();\n127\t    unsafe { cuda_memcpy::<true, true>(\n128\t        sel_buf_a.as_mut_ptr().add(off) as *mut c_void,\n129\t        m.buffer().as_ptr() as *const c_void, bytes); }\n130\t    sel_offsets.push(off);\n131\t    off += m.buffer().len();\n132\t}\n133\tfor (s, &o) in sel_slices.iter_mut().zip(&sel_offsets) { s.offset = o; }\n134\t\n135\t// Free original DeviceMatrix vectors (reclaim GPU memory)\n136\tdrop(std::mem::take(&mut self.mat_evals_per_trace));\n137\tdrop(std::mem::take(&mut self.sels_per_trace));\n138\t```\n139\t\n140\t**Why**: The initial D2D pack costs ~2-3ms but enables uniform code for all rounds (no round-1 special case). The ~2-3ms is amortized across 24 rounds of zero-alloc folding, netting 10-17ms improvement.\n141\t\n142\t### 3. Replace fold_mle_evals with ping-pong implementation\n143\t\n144\t**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/mod.rs`\n145\t\n146\tNew method `fold_mle_evals_pingpong` replaces the old `fold_mle_evals`:\n147\t\n148\t```rust\n149\tfn fold_mle_evals_pingpong(\n150\t    &mut self, round: usize, r_round: EF,\n151\t    mat_sizes: &mut [(usize, usize)], mat_offsets: &mut [usize],\n152\t    buf_a: &mut DeviceBuffer<EF>, buf_b: &mut DeviceBuffer<EF>,\n153\t    sel_sizes: &mut [(usize, usize)], sel_offsets: &mut [usize],\n154\t    sel_a: &mut DeviceBuffer<EF>, sel_b: &mut DeviceBuffer<EF>,\n155\t) -> Result<(), LogupZerocheckError> {\n156\t    // Helper: fold one set of matrices (mat_evals or sels)\n157\t    let fold_set = |sizes: &mut [(usize, usize)], offsets: &mut [usize],\n158\t                     src: &DeviceBuffer<EF>, dst: &mut DeviceBuffer<EF>| -> Result<(), _> {\n159\t        let num_foldable = sizes.partition_point(|(h, _)| *h > 1);\n160\t        if num_foldable == 0 { return Ok(()); }\n161\t\n162\t        let input_ptrs: Vec<_> = (0..num_foldable)\n163\t            .map(|i| unsafe { src.as_ptr().add(offsets[i]) })\n164\t            .collect();\n165\t        let mut out_off = 0usize;\n166\t        let output_ptrs: Vec<_> = (0..num_foldable)\n167\t            .map(|i| {\n168\t                let ptr = unsafe { dst.as_mut_ptr().add(out_off) };\n169\t                out_off += (sizes[i].0 / 2) * sizes[i].1;\n170\t                ptr\n171\t            })\n172\t            .collect();\n173\t        let log_heights: Vec<u8> = (0..num_foldable)\n174\t            .map(|i| (sizes[i].0 / 2).ilog2() as u8)\n175\t            .collect();\n176\t        let widths: Vec<u32> = (0..num_foldable)\n177\t            .map(|i| sizes[i].1 as u32)\n178\t            .collect();\n179\t        let max_cells = (0..num_foldable)\n180\t            .map(|i| (sizes[i].0 / 2) * sizes[i].1)\n181\t            .max()\n182\t            .unwrap_or(0);\n183\t\n184\t        let d_in = input_ptrs.to_device()?;\n185\t        let d_out = output_ptrs.to_device()?;\n186\t        let d_h = log_heights.to_device()?;\n187\t        let d_w = widths.to_device()?;\n188\t\n189\t        unsafe {\n190\t            batch_fold_mle(&d_in, &d_out, &d_w, num_foldable as u32, &d_h,\n191\t                           max_cells as u32, r_round)?;\n192\t        }\n193\t\n194\t        // Update sizes and offsets for next round\n195\t        out_off = 0;\n196\t        for i in 0..num_foldable {\n197\t            sizes[i].0 /= 2;\n198\t            offsets[i] = out_off;\n199\t            out_off += sizes[i].0 * sizes[i].1;\n200\t        }\n201\t        // Copy non-foldable (height=1) matrices to maintain contiguous layout\n202\t        for i in num_foldable..sizes.len() {\n203\t            let cells = sizes[i].0 * sizes[i].1;\n204\t            unsafe {\n205\t                cuda_memcpy_d2d(dst.as_mut_ptr().add(out_off),\n206\t                               src.as_ptr().add(offsets[i]), cells);\n207\t            }\n208\t            offsets[i] = out_off;\n209\t            out_off += cells;\n210\t        }\n211\t        Ok(())\n212\t    };\n213\t\n214\t    fold_set(mat_sizes, mat_offsets, buf_a, buf_b)?;\n215\t    std::mem::swap(buf_a, buf_b);\n216\t\n217\t    fold_set(sel_sizes, sel_offsets, sel_a, sel_b)?;\n218\t    std::mem::swap(sel_a, sel_b);\n219\t\n220\t    // eq_xis, eq_ns, eq_sharp_ns updates — unchanged from current code (lines 2080-2089)\n221\t    for tree in self.eq_xis.values_mut() {\n222\t        if tree.layers.len() > 1 { tree.layers.pop(); }\n223\t    }\n224\t    let xi = self.xi[self.l_skip + round - 1];\n225\t    let eq_r = eval_eq_mle(&[xi], &[r_round]);\n226\t    self.eq_ns.push(self.eq_ns[round - 1] * eq_r);\n227\t    self.eq_sharp_ns.push(self.eq_sharp_ns[round - 1] * eq_r);\n228\t    Ok(())\n229\t}\n230\t```\n231\t\n232\t### 4. Update sumcheck_polys_batch_eval to use buffer views\n233\t\n234\t**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/mod.rs`\n235\t\n236\tUse `MatSlice` and prefix sums to index into the ping-pong buffer. For each `trace_idx`, the flat range of matrices is `mat_per_trace_prefix[trace_idx]..mat_per_trace_prefix[trace_idx] + mat_per_trace_counts[trace_idx]`.\n237\t\n238\tAll call sites that access `self.mat_evals_per_trace[trace_idx][mat_idx]` or `self.sels_per_trace[trace_idx]` need updating:\n239\t\n240\t**Case A.1 (late eval, lines 1601-1638)**: Accesses `mats[0]` for preprocessed and `mats[first_main_idx..]` for mains:\n241\t```rust\n242\tlet flat_base = mat_per_trace_prefix[trace_idx];\n243\t// Preprocessed (mat index 0 if has_preprocessed)\n244\tlet prep_ptr = if has_preprocessed {\n245\t    let s = &mat_slices[flat_base];\n246\t    MainMatrixPtrs { data: unsafe { buf.as_ptr().add(s.offset) }, air_width: air_width_for_mat(need_rot, s.width) }\n247\t} else { ... };\n248\t// Mains (indices first_main_idx..)\n249\tlet main_ptrs: Vec<_> = (flat_base + first_main_idx..flat_base + mat_per_trace_counts[trace_idx])\n250\t    .map(|i| {\n251\t        let s = &mat_slices[i];\n252\t        MainMatrixPtrs { data: unsafe { buf.as_ptr().add(s.offset) }, air_width: air_width_for_mat(need_rot, s.width) }\n253\t    }).collect();\n254\t```\n255\t\n256\t**Case B (early eval, lines 1649-1685)**: Column pointer collection iterates columns:\n257\t```rust\n258\t// For sels:\n259\tlet sel = &sel_slices[trace_idx];\n260\tlet sel_ptr = unsafe { sel_buf.as_ptr().add(sel.offset) };\n261\tfor col in 0..sel.width {\n262\t    all_columns.push(unsafe { sel_ptr.add(col * sel.height) });  // column-major stride\n263\t}\n264\t// For each mat in trace:\n265\tfor i in flat_base..flat_base + mat_per_trace_counts[trace_idx] {\n266\t    let s = &mat_slices[i];\n267\t    let mat_ptr = unsafe { buf.as_ptr().add(s.offset) };\n268\t    for col in 0..s.width {\n269\t        all_columns.push(unsafe { mat_ptr.add(col * s.height) });\n270\t    }\n271\t}\n272\t```\n273\t\n274\t**Key invariant**: Within each matrix's region in the ping-pong buffer, the column-major layout is preserved exactly (columns spaced by `height` elements) because the D2D/fold copies raw bytes in the same layout.\n275\t\n276\t**Phase 3 width accesses (lines 1749-1767)**: Replace `mats[0].width()` with `mat_slices[flat_base].width` and iteration over `mats[first_main_idx..]` with flat-index iteration using `mat_slices[flat_base + first_main_idx..].iter().map(|s| s.width)`.\n277\t\n278\t### 5. Update into_column_openings\n279\t\n280\t**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/mod.rs`\n281\t\n282\tThe current `into_column_openings` (line 2098) does more than simple D2H: it splits doubled-width matrices for `need_rot` AIRs, reorders common_main to front, and interleaves plain/rotated columns. This logic MUST be preserved.\n283\t\n284\t**Approach**: Before calling the existing `into_column_openings`, reconstruct `self.mat_evals_per_trace` and `self.sels_per_trace` from the ping-pong buffer as host-side data, then let the existing logic operate unchanged.\n285\t\n286\t```rust\n287\t// Bulk D2H the entire ping-pong buffer\n288\tlet host_mat_buf = {\n289\t    let total_cells = mat_slices.iter().map(|s| s.height * s.width).sum::<usize>();\n290\t    let view = std::mem::ManuallyDrop::new(\n291\t        unsafe { DeviceBuffer::<EF>::from_raw_parts(mat_buf_a.as_ptr() as *mut EF, total_cells) }\n292\t    );\n293\t    view.to_host().map_err(LogupZerocheckError::MemCopy)?\n294\t};\n295\t\n296\t// Reconstruct per-trace DeviceMatrix from host data (for the existing into_column_openings logic).\n297\t// The existing code calls m.to_host() anyway, so we can short-circuit by providing host-side\n298\t// ColMajorMatrix views directly. Modify into_column_openings to accept either:\n299\t//   (a) Pre-fetched host data slices, or\n300\t//   (b) Reconstruct DeviceMatrix with ManuallyDrop from the ping-pong buffer.\n301\t//\n302\t// Simplest: reconstruct self.mat_evals_per_trace as ManuallyDrop<DeviceMatrix> views.\n303\t// Since DeviceMatrix wraps Arc<DeviceBuffer>, and we need non-owning views,\n304\t// the cleanest path is to do a per-matrix D2H at this point using ManuallyDrop<DeviceBuffer>:\n305\t\n306\tlet mut flat_idx = 0;\n307\tself.mat_evals_per_trace = mat_per_trace_counts.iter().map(|&count| {\n308\t    (0..count).map(|_| {\n309\t        let s = &mat_slices[flat_idx];\n310\t        flat_idx += 1;\n311\t        // Slice host buffer into a DeviceMatrix-compatible form.\n312\t        // Use ManuallyDrop to create a non-owning DeviceBuffer view for D2H.\n313\t        let ptr = unsafe { mat_buf_a.as_ptr().add(s.offset) } as *mut EF;\n314\t        let view = std::mem::ManuallyDrop::new(\n315\t            unsafe { DeviceBuffer::<EF>::from_raw_parts(ptr, s.height * s.width) }\n316\t        );\n317\t        // Construct DeviceMatrix from the non-owning buffer. Since into_column_openings\n318\t        // immediately calls to_host(), the DeviceMatrix is short-lived.\n319\t        DeviceMatrix::<EF>::from_non_owning(view, s.height, s.width)\n320\t    }).collect()\n321\t}).collect();\n322\t// Same for sels_per_trace...\n323\t```\n324\t\n325\t**Preferred approach (per final review)**: Since `DeviceMatrix` wraps `Arc<DeviceBuffer>` which prevents non-owning construction, the cleanest path is:\n326\t1. Do a single bulk D2H of the entire ping-pong buffer to host memory\n327\t2. Slice the host data per-matrix using `mat_slices` offsets/sizes\n328\t3. Extract the split/reorder/need_rot logic from the existing `into_column_openings` into a helper that operates on `(host_data: &[EF], height, width, need_rot)` tuples\n329\t4. Call the helper per-trace to produce the final column openings\n330\t\n331\tThe existing `into_column_openings` logic is ~50 lines of straightforward host-side work (matrix transpose, width splitting, column interleaving). Extracting it avoids the `Arc<DeviceBuffer>` ownership issue entirely while preserving correctness.\n332\t\n333\t### 6. Memory accounting for save_memory path\n334\t\n335\t**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/mod.rs`\n336\t\n337\tLines 2067-2075 adjust `memory_limit_bytes` based on mat_evals buffer sizes. Replace with:\n338\t```rust\n339\tif self.save_memory {\n340\t    let current_cells: usize = mat_sizes.iter().map(|(h,w)| h * w).sum();\n341\t    self.memory_limit_bytes = self.gkr_mem_contribution\n342\t        .saturating_sub(current_cells * size_of::<EF>());\n343\t}\n344\t```\n345\t\n346\t## Invariants\n347\t\n348\t1. **Fold kernel correctness**: batch_fold_mle receives identical (input_ptr, output_ptr, height, width) data. Only the source of pointers changes.\n349\t\n350\t2. **Buffer capacity**: Buffer A starts at total_cells. After round 1, data is in B at total_cells/2. After swap, A holds total_cells/2 data. B (now old A, full capacity) is always large enough for the output.\n351\t\n352\t3. **Non-foldable matrices**: D2D-copied from src to dst each round to maintain contiguous layout. Cost: sum of (width) elements for all height-1 matrices. Even with 1400 matrices of average width 50, total copy is ~70K elements × 16 bytes = 560KB — well within a single async D2D latency (~0.1ms).\n353\t\n354\t4. **Pointer array uploads**: Still 4 H2D uploads per fold call (same as current code). These are small Vecs (~800 elements × 8 bytes = 6.4KB).\n355\t\n356\t5. **No APC 0 regression**: APC 0 has fewer matrices (~99 traces × 1-3 each ≈ 150 matrices). Ping-pong setup D2D is proportionally smaller. Allocation savings are proportionally smaller but still positive.\n357\t\n358\t6. **into_column_openings correctness**: The existing split/reorder/need_rot logic is preserved by reconstructing `mat_evals_per_trace` and `sels_per_trace` from the ping-pong buffer before calling the existing `into_column_openings` method. `ManuallyDrop<DeviceBuffer>` prevents double-free on sub-buffer pointers. If `DeviceMatrix` can't be constructed non-owningly, the fallback refactors `into_column_openings` to accept `(ptr, height, width)` tuples.\n359\t\n360\t## Measurement Plan\n361\t\n362\t1. Build and run benchmark for APC {0, 300}\n363\t2. Compare MLE Rounds time at APC 300: 173ms → expect ~155-160ms\n364\t3. Compare STARK excl trace: 1302ms → expect ~1282-1287ms\n365\t4. Verify APC 0 no regression\n366\t5. Verify correctness (proof verification succeeds)\n367\t\n368\t## Rollback Criteria\n369\t\n370\t- MLE Rounds improvement at APC 300 <10ms\n371\t- STARK excl trace improvement at APC 300 <10ms\n372\t- APC 0 regression >10ms\n373\t- Correctness failure\n374\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d2c41f48-5b80-4de8-b307-355a7b8c0ec2","uuid":"06f117d5-3fef-494a-a6b7-476df26f99f5","timestamp":"2026-04-14T15:09:27.144Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/georg/stark-backend/autoopt-results/2026-04-14-1630-pingpong-mle-fold-buffers/plan.md","content":"# Plan: Ping-Pong MLE Fold Buffers\n\n## Goal\n\nEliminate ~67K per-benchmark DeviceMatrix allocations and ~67K frees in the constraints-phase MLE fold (`fold_mle_evals`) by replacing them with two pre-allocated contiguous device buffers used in a ping-pong pattern. MLE Rounds at APC 300 take 173ms, of which ~15-20ms is CUDA memory pool API overhead from these allocations (confirmed by the bulk-alloc-mle-fold-buffers task which recovered 13ms with a heavier ArenaMatrix approach). This cleaner implementation avoids the ArenaMatrix/MatrixRef/FoldArena type complexity of the previous attempt.\n\n## Current Code Path\n\n### MLE Rounds loop\n`crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/mod.rs:631-648`\n```rust\nfor round in 1..=n_max {\n    let sp_round_evals = prover.sumcheck_polys_batch_eval(round, r[round - 1])?;\n    // ... transcript observe, sample r_round ...\n    prover.fold_mle_evals(round, r_round)?;\n}\n```\n\n### fold_mle_evals\n`crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/mod.rs:1999-2091`\n\nContains `batch_fold` closure (lines 2002-2048):\n1. Counts foldable matrices (height > 1) via `partition_point` (line 2003)\n2. Allocates output: `DeviceMatrix::<EF>::with_capacity(output_height, width)` per foldable matrix (line 2014) → `cudaMallocAsync`\n3. Collects input/output pointer Vecs (lines 2019-2027)\n4. Uploads 4 pointer arrays to device (lines 2029-2032)\n5. Launches single `batch_fold_mle` kernel (lines 2034-2044)\n6. Returns new output matrices, dropping old inputs → `cudaFreeAsync` each\n\nCalled twice per round:\n- `mat_evals_per_trace` (lines 2050-2066): ~800 matrices at APC 300\n- `sels_per_trace` (line 2078): ~623 matrices\n\nPer round: ~1400 allocs + ~1400 frees = ~2800 CUDA API calls.\nPer benchmark (24 rounds × 2 segments): ~134K API calls (~67K allocs, ~67K frees).\nAt 0.3-0.5μs per call: **20-33ms total overhead** (previous task confirmed 13ms recovery, suggesting ~15-20ms was actual overhead).\n\n### sumcheck_polys_batch_eval\n`crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/mod.rs:1536-1922`\n\nReads `self.mat_evals_per_trace[trace_idx][mat_idx]` and `self.sels_per_trace[trace_idx]` to get `.buffer().as_ptr()`, `.height()`, `.width()`. These are the DeviceMatrix objects being replaced.\n\n### into_column_openings\n`crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/mod.rs:2098+`\n\nCalls `m.to_host()` on each final DeviceMatrix to get column openings. Must still work after replacement.\n\n## Changes\n\n### 1. Add ping-pong buffer state to LogupZerocheckGpu\n\n**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/mod.rs`\n\nAdd fields to `LogupZerocheckGpu`:\n```rust\n/// Ping-pong buffer A for mat_evals fold (current round's data)\nmat_fold_buf_a: DeviceBuffer<EF>,\n/// Ping-pong buffer B for mat_evals fold (next round's output)\nmat_fold_buf_b: DeviceBuffer<EF>,\n/// Per-matrix (height, width) — updated each fold (height halves)\nmat_fold_sizes: Vec<(usize, usize)>,\n/// Per-matrix byte offset within the current buffer\nmat_fold_offsets: Vec<usize>,\n/// Per-trace count of matrices (to reconstruct nested structure)\nmat_per_trace_counts: Vec<usize>,\n/// Same for sels\nsel_fold_buf_a: DeviceBuffer<EF>,\nsel_fold_buf_b: DeviceBuffer<EF>,\nsel_fold_sizes: Vec<(usize, usize)>,\nsel_fold_offsets: Vec<usize>,\n```\n\n### 2. Initialize ping-pong buffers before MLE loop\n\n**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/mod.rs`\n\nAfter `fold_ple_evals` (line 617) and before the MLE loop (line 631), compute layout metadata and allocate buffer B only (buffer A is the original DeviceMatrix data, used in round 1):\n\n```rust\n// Compute per-matrix metadata for ping-pong layout.\nstruct MatSlice { offset: usize, height: usize, width: usize }\n\nlet mat_slices: Vec<MatSlice> = self.mat_evals_per_trace.iter()\n    .flatten()\n    .map(|m| MatSlice { offset: 0 /* filled after round 1 */, height: m.height(), width: m.width() })\n    .collect();\nlet mat_per_trace_counts: Vec<usize> = self.mat_evals_per_trace.iter()\n    .map(|v| v.len()).collect();\n// Prefix sums for per-trace indexing into flat array\nlet mat_per_trace_prefix: Vec<usize> = mat_per_trace_counts.iter()\n    .scan(0, |acc, &c| { let v = *acc; *acc += c; Some(v) }).collect();\nlet mat_total: usize = mat_slices.iter().map(|s| s.height * s.width).sum();\n\nlet sel_slices: Vec<MatSlice> = self.sels_per_trace.iter()\n    .map(|m| MatSlice { offset: 0, height: m.height(), width: m.width() }).collect();\nlet sel_total: usize = sel_slices.iter().map(|s| s.height * s.width).sum();\n\n// Allocate ONE ping-pong buffer (B). Round 1 reads from original DeviceMatrix data,\n// writes into buffer B. Then drop originals and allocate buffer A for round 2 output.\nlet mut mat_buf_b = DeviceBuffer::<EF>::with_capacity(mat_total);\nlet mut sel_buf_b = DeviceBuffer::<EF>::with_capacity(sel_total);\n```\n\n**D2D copy primitive**: For all D2D copies throughout this plan, use the existing `cuda_memcpy::<true, true>(dst as *mut c_void, src as *const c_void, count * size_of::<EF>())` from `crates/cuda-common/src/copy.rs:42`. No new helper function needed.\n\nPack mat_evals and sels into their respective buffer A via D2D copies:\n\n```rust\nlet mut mat_offsets = Vec::with_capacity(mat_slices.len());\nlet mut off = 0usize;\nfor m in self.mat_evals_per_trace.iter().flatten() {\n    let bytes = m.buffer().len() * std::mem::size_of::<EF>();\n    unsafe { cuda_memcpy::<true, true>(\n        mat_buf_a.as_mut_ptr().add(off) as *mut c_void,\n        m.buffer().as_ptr() as *const c_void, bytes); }\n    mat_offsets.push(off);\n    off += m.buffer().len();\n}\n// Update mat_slices with computed offsets\nfor (s, &o) in mat_slices.iter_mut().zip(&mat_offsets) { s.offset = o; }\n\n// Same for sels into sel_buf_a\nlet mut sel_offsets = Vec::with_capacity(sel_slices.len());\noff = 0;\nfor m in &self.sels_per_trace {\n    let bytes = m.buffer().len() * std::mem::size_of::<EF>();\n    unsafe { cuda_memcpy::<true, true>(\n        sel_buf_a.as_mut_ptr().add(off) as *mut c_void,\n        m.buffer().as_ptr() as *const c_void, bytes); }\n    sel_offsets.push(off);\n    off += m.buffer().len();\n}\nfor (s, &o) in sel_slices.iter_mut().zip(&sel_offsets) { s.offset = o; }\n\n// Free original DeviceMatrix vectors (reclaim GPU memory)\ndrop(std::mem::take(&mut self.mat_evals_per_trace));\ndrop(std::mem::take(&mut self.sels_per_trace));\n```\n\n**Why**: The initial D2D pack costs ~2-3ms but enables uniform code for all rounds (no round-1 special case). The ~2-3ms is amortized across 24 rounds of zero-alloc folding, netting 10-17ms improvement.\n\n### 3. Replace fold_mle_evals with ping-pong implementation\n\n**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/mod.rs`\n\nNew method `fold_mle_evals_pingpong` replaces the old `fold_mle_evals`:\n\n```rust\nfn fold_mle_evals_pingpong(\n    &mut self, round: usize, r_round: EF,\n    mat_sizes: &mut [(usize, usize)], mat_offsets: &mut [usize],\n    buf_a: &mut DeviceBuffer<EF>, buf_b: &mut DeviceBuffer<EF>,\n    sel_sizes: &mut [(usize, usize)], sel_offsets: &mut [usize],\n    sel_a: &mut DeviceBuffer<EF>, sel_b: &mut DeviceBuffer<EF>,\n) -> Result<(), LogupZerocheckError> {\n    // Helper: fold one set of matrices (mat_evals or sels)\n    let fold_set = |sizes: &mut [(usize, usize)], offsets: &mut [usize],\n                     src: &DeviceBuffer<EF>, dst: &mut DeviceBuffer<EF>| -> Result<(), _> {\n        let num_foldable = sizes.partition_point(|(h, _)| *h > 1);\n        if num_foldable == 0 { return Ok(()); }\n\n        let input_ptrs: Vec<_> = (0..num_foldable)\n            .map(|i| unsafe { src.as_ptr().add(offsets[i]) })\n            .collect();\n        let mut out_off = 0usize;\n        let output_ptrs: Vec<_> = (0..num_foldable)\n            .map(|i| {\n                let ptr = unsafe { dst.as_mut_ptr().add(out_off) };\n                out_off += (sizes[i].0 / 2) * sizes[i].1;\n                ptr\n            })\n            .collect();\n        let log_heights: Vec<u8> = (0..num_foldable)\n            .map(|i| (sizes[i].0 / 2).ilog2() as u8)\n            .collect();\n        let widths: Vec<u32> = (0..num_foldable)\n            .map(|i| sizes[i].1 as u32)\n            .collect();\n        let max_cells = (0..num_foldable)\n            .map(|i| (sizes[i].0 / 2) * sizes[i].1)\n            .max()\n            .unwrap_or(0);\n\n        let d_in = input_ptrs.to_device()?;\n        let d_out = output_ptrs.to_device()?;\n        let d_h = log_heights.to_device()?;\n        let d_w = widths.to_device()?;\n\n        unsafe {\n            batch_fold_mle(&d_in, &d_out, &d_w, num_foldable as u32, &d_h,\n                           max_cells as u32, r_round)?;\n        }\n\n        // Update sizes and offsets for next round\n        out_off = 0;\n        for i in 0..num_foldable {\n            sizes[i].0 /= 2;\n            offsets[i] = out_off;\n            out_off += sizes[i].0 * sizes[i].1;\n        }\n        // Copy non-foldable (height=1) matrices to maintain contiguous layout\n        for i in num_foldable..sizes.len() {\n            let cells = sizes[i].0 * sizes[i].1;\n            unsafe {\n                cuda_memcpy_d2d(dst.as_mut_ptr().add(out_off),\n                               src.as_ptr().add(offsets[i]), cells);\n            }\n            offsets[i] = out_off;\n            out_off += cells;\n        }\n        Ok(())\n    };\n\n    fold_set(mat_sizes, mat_offsets, buf_a, buf_b)?;\n    std::mem::swap(buf_a, buf_b);\n\n    fold_set(sel_sizes, sel_offsets, sel_a, sel_b)?;\n    std::mem::swap(sel_a, sel_b);\n\n    // eq_xis, eq_ns, eq_sharp_ns updates — unchanged from current code (lines 2080-2089)\n    for tree in self.eq_xis.values_mut() {\n        if tree.layers.len() > 1 { tree.layers.pop(); }\n    }\n    let xi = self.xi[self.l_skip + round - 1];\n    let eq_r = eval_eq_mle(&[xi], &[r_round]);\n    self.eq_ns.push(self.eq_ns[round - 1] * eq_r);\n    self.eq_sharp_ns.push(self.eq_sharp_ns[round - 1] * eq_r);\n    Ok(())\n}\n```\n\n### 4. Update sumcheck_polys_batch_eval to use buffer views\n\n**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/mod.rs`\n\nUse `MatSlice` and prefix sums to index into the ping-pong buffer. For each `trace_idx`, the flat range of matrices is `mat_per_trace_prefix[trace_idx]..mat_per_trace_prefix[trace_idx] + mat_per_trace_counts[trace_idx]`.\n\nAll call sites that access `self.mat_evals_per_trace[trace_idx][mat_idx]` or `self.sels_per_trace[trace_idx]` need updating:\n\n**Case A.1 (late eval, lines 1601-1638)**: Accesses `mats[0]` for preprocessed and `mats[first_main_idx..]` for mains:\n```rust\nlet flat_base = mat_per_trace_prefix[trace_idx];\n// Preprocessed (mat index 0 if has_preprocessed)\nlet prep_ptr = if has_preprocessed {\n    let s = &mat_slices[flat_base];\n    MainMatrixPtrs { data: unsafe { buf.as_ptr().add(s.offset) }, air_width: air_width_for_mat(need_rot, s.width) }\n} else { ... };\n// Mains (indices first_main_idx..)\nlet main_ptrs: Vec<_> = (flat_base + first_main_idx..flat_base + mat_per_trace_counts[trace_idx])\n    .map(|i| {\n        let s = &mat_slices[i];\n        MainMatrixPtrs { data: unsafe { buf.as_ptr().add(s.offset) }, air_width: air_width_for_mat(need_rot, s.width) }\n    }).collect();\n```\n\n**Case B (early eval, lines 1649-1685)**: Column pointer collection iterates columns:\n```rust\n// For sels:\nlet sel = &sel_slices[trace_idx];\nlet sel_ptr = unsafe { sel_buf.as_ptr().add(sel.offset) };\nfor col in 0..sel.width {\n    all_columns.push(unsafe { sel_ptr.add(col * sel.height) });  // column-major stride\n}\n// For each mat in trace:\nfor i in flat_base..flat_base + mat_per_trace_counts[trace_idx] {\n    let s = &mat_slices[i];\n    let mat_ptr = unsafe { buf.as_ptr().add(s.offset) };\n    for col in 0..s.width {\n        all_columns.push(unsafe { mat_ptr.add(col * s.height) });\n    }\n}\n```\n\n**Key invariant**: Within each matrix's region in the ping-pong buffer, the column-major layout is preserved exactly (columns spaced by `height` elements) because the D2D/fold copies raw bytes in the same layout.\n\n**Phase 3 width accesses (lines 1749-1767)**: Replace `mats[0].width()` with `mat_slices[flat_base].width` and iteration over `mats[first_main_idx..]` with flat-index iteration using `mat_slices[flat_base + first_main_idx..].iter().map(|s| s.width)`.\n\n### 5. Update into_column_openings\n\n**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/mod.rs`\n\nThe current `into_column_openings` (line 2098) does more than simple D2H: it splits doubled-width matrices for `need_rot` AIRs, reorders common_main to front, and interleaves plain/rotated columns. This logic MUST be preserved.\n\n**Approach**: Before calling the existing `into_column_openings`, reconstruct `self.mat_evals_per_trace` and `self.sels_per_trace` from the ping-pong buffer as host-side data, then let the existing logic operate unchanged.\n\n```rust\n// Bulk D2H the entire ping-pong buffer\nlet host_mat_buf = {\n    let total_cells = mat_slices.iter().map(|s| s.height * s.width).sum::<usize>();\n    let view = std::mem::ManuallyDrop::new(\n        unsafe { DeviceBuffer::<EF>::from_raw_parts(mat_buf_a.as_ptr() as *mut EF, total_cells) }\n    );\n    view.to_host().map_err(LogupZerocheckError::MemCopy)?\n};\n\n// Reconstruct per-trace DeviceMatrix from host data (for the existing into_column_openings logic).\n// The existing code calls m.to_host() anyway, so we can short-circuit by providing host-side\n// ColMajorMatrix views directly. Modify into_column_openings to accept either:\n//   (a) Pre-fetched host data slices, or\n//   (b) Reconstruct DeviceMatrix with ManuallyDrop from the ping-pong buffer.\n//\n// Simplest: reconstruct self.mat_evals_per_trace as ManuallyDrop<DeviceMatrix> views.\n// Since DeviceMatrix wraps Arc<DeviceBuffer>, and we need non-owning views,\n// the cleanest path is to do a per-matrix D2H at this point using ManuallyDrop<DeviceBuffer>:\n\nlet mut flat_idx = 0;\nself.mat_evals_per_trace = mat_per_trace_counts.iter().map(|&count| {\n    (0..count).map(|_| {\n        let s = &mat_slices[flat_idx];\n        flat_idx += 1;\n        // Slice host buffer into a DeviceMatrix-compatible form.\n        // Use ManuallyDrop to create a non-owning DeviceBuffer view for D2H.\n        let ptr = unsafe { mat_buf_a.as_ptr().add(s.offset) } as *mut EF;\n        let view = std::mem::ManuallyDrop::new(\n            unsafe { DeviceBuffer::<EF>::from_raw_parts(ptr, s.height * s.width) }\n        );\n        // Construct DeviceMatrix from the non-owning buffer. Since into_column_openings\n        // immediately calls to_host(), the DeviceMatrix is short-lived.\n        DeviceMatrix::<EF>::from_non_owning(view, s.height, s.width)\n    }).collect()\n}).collect();\n// Same for sels_per_trace...\n```\n\n**Preferred approach (per final review)**: Since `DeviceMatrix` wraps `Arc<DeviceBuffer>` which prevents non-owning construction, the cleanest path is:\n1. Do a single bulk D2H of the entire ping-pong buffer to host memory\n2. Slice the host data per-matrix using `mat_slices` offsets/sizes\n3. Extract the split/reorder/need_rot logic from the existing `into_column_openings` into a helper that operates on `(host_data: &[EF], height, width, need_rot)` tuples\n4. Call the helper per-trace to produce the final column openings\n\nThe existing `into_column_openings` logic is ~50 lines of straightforward host-side work (matrix transpose, width splitting, column interleaving). Extracting it avoids the `Arc<DeviceBuffer>` ownership issue entirely while preserving correctness.\n\n### 6. Memory accounting for save_memory path\n\n**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/mod.rs`\n\nLines 2067-2075 adjust `memory_limit_bytes` based on mat_evals buffer sizes. Replace with:\n```rust\nif self.save_memory {\n    let current_cells: usize = mat_sizes.iter().map(|(h,w)| h * w).sum();\n    self.memory_limit_bytes = self.gkr_mem_contribution\n        .saturating_sub(current_cells * size_of::<EF>());\n}\n```\n\n## Invariants\n\n1. **Fold kernel correctness**: batch_fold_mle receives identical (input_ptr, output_ptr, height, width) data. Only the source of pointers changes.\n\n2. **Buffer capacity**: Buffer A starts at total_cells. After round 1, data is in B at total_cells/2. After swap, A holds total_cells/2 data. B (now old A, full capacity) is always large enough for the output.\n\n3. **Non-foldable matrices**: D2D-copied from src to dst each round to maintain contiguous layout. Cost: sum of (width) elements for all height-1 matrices. Even with 1400 matrices of average width 50, total copy is ~70K elements × 16 bytes = 560KB — well within a single async D2D latency (~0.1ms).\n\n4. **Pointer array uploads**: Still 4 H2D uploads per fold call (same as current code). These are small Vecs (~800 elements × 8 bytes = 6.4KB).\n\n5. **No APC 0 regression**: APC 0 has fewer matrices (~99 traces × 1-3 each ≈ 150 matrices). Ping-pong setup D2D is proportionally smaller. Allocation savings are proportionally smaller but still positive.\n\n6. **into_column_openings correctness**: The existing split/reorder/need_rot logic is preserved by reconstructing `mat_evals_per_trace` and `sels_per_trace` from the ping-pong buffer before calling the existing `into_column_openings` method. `ManuallyDrop<DeviceBuffer>` prevents double-free on sub-buffer pointers. If `DeviceMatrix` can't be constructed non-owningly, the fallback refactors `into_column_openings` to accept `(ptr, height, width)` tuples.\n\n## Measurement Plan\n\n1. Build and run benchmark for APC {0, 300}\n2. Compare MLE Rounds time at APC 300: 173ms → expect ~155-160ms\n3. Compare STARK excl trace: 1302ms → expect ~1282-1287ms\n4. Verify APC 0 no regression\n5. Verify correctness (proof verification succeeds)\n\n## Rollback Criteria\n\n- MLE Rounds improvement at APC 300 <10ms\n- STARK excl trace improvement at APC 300 <10ms\n- APC 0 regression >10ms\n- Correctness failure\n","numLines":374,"startLine":1,"totalLines":374}}}
