{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Rb1ToMNTPVjYSi67xrAiL7","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Excellent! Now let me create a comprehensive summary with all the file paths and line numbers:\n\n## Summary\n\nI've thoroughly explored the repository and found all the requested types and functions. Here's the complete breakdown:\n\n### 1. **DeviceBuffer<T> - Type Definition**\n\n**Location:** `/home/georg/stark-backend/crates/cuda-common/src/d_buffer.rs`, lines 18-22\n\n```rust\n#[repr(C)]\npub struct DeviceBuffer<T> {\n    ptr: *mut T,\n    len: usize,\n}\n```\n\n**Key Methods:**\n\n| Method | Location | Line | Signature |\n|--------|----------|------|-----------|\n| `with_capacity` | d_buffer.rs | 60 | `pub fn with_capacity(len: usize) -> Self` |\n| `as_ptr` | d_buffer.rs | 125 | `pub fn as_ptr(&self) -> *const T` |\n| `as_mut_ptr` | d_buffer.rs | 120 | `pub fn as_mut_ptr(&self) -> *mut T` |\n| `from_raw_parts` (unsafe) | d_buffer.rs | 55 | `pub unsafe fn from_raw_parts(ptr: *mut T, len: usize) -> Self` |\n| `to_host` | d_buffer.rs | 101-125 | Trait method via `MemCopyD2H<T>` impl |\n| `len` | d_buffer.rs | 110 | `pub fn len(&self) -> usize` |\n\n**Ownership Model:**\n- DeviceBuffer **owns** the device memory it points to\n- Has a `Drop` impl (line 169) that calls `d_free()` on the raw pointer\n- NOT wrapped in Arc - it's a direct owner\n- Cannot be cloned (move-only semantics)\n- Send + Sync (unsafe impls at line 36-37)\n\n**View Creation (Non-owning):**\n- Use `view()` method (line 161) to create a `DeviceBufferView` without owning the data\n- `DeviceBufferView` is `Copy + Clone` and holds `*const c_void` pointer + size (lines 29-34)\n\n---\n\n### 2. **DeviceMatrix<T> - Type Definition**\n\n**Location:** `/home/georg/stark-backend/crates/cuda-backend/src/base.rs`, lines 6-10\n\n```rust\npub struct DeviceMatrix<T> {\n    buffer: Arc<DeviceBuffer<T>>,\n    height: usize,\n    width: usize,\n}\n```\n\n**Key Methods:**\n\n| Method | Location | Line | Signature |\n|--------|----------|------|-----------|\n| `with_capacity` | base.rs | 56 | `pub fn with_capacity(height: usize, width: usize) -> Self` |\n| `buffer()` | base.rs | 72 | `pub fn buffer(&self) -> &DeviceBuffer<T>` |\n| `height()` | base.rs | 88 | `fn height(&self) -> usize` (via MatrixDimensions trait) |\n| `width()` | base.rs | 93 | `fn width(&self) -> usize` (via MatrixDimensions trait) |\n| `new` | base.rs | 36 | `pub fn new(buffer: Arc<DeviceBuffer<T>>, height: usize, width: usize) -> Self` |\n| `as_view` | base.rs | 80 | `pub fn as_view(&self) -> DeviceMatrixView<'_, T>` |\n| `strong_count` | base.rs | 76 | `pub fn strong_count(&self) -> usize` (returns Arc ref count) |\n\n**Ownership Model:**\n- **Arc-wrapped buffer** - shared ownership via `Arc<DeviceBuffer<T>>`\n- Implements `Clone` (line 15) - cloning increments Arc ref count\n- Implements `Send + Sync` (unsafe impls at lines 12-13)\n- Has custom `Drop` impl (lines 25-33) that logs ref counts\n- **Use `as_view()` to create non-owning references** via `DeviceMatrixView<'a, T>` (lifetime-bounded view)\n\n**DeviceMatrixView (Non-owning View):**\n- Location: base.rs, lines 117-156\n- Uses `PhantomData<&'a T>` to enforce lifetime boundaries (line 122)\n- Unsafe constructor `from_raw_parts` (line 132): `pub unsafe fn from_raw_parts(ptr: *const T, height: usize, width: usize) -> Self`\n- Copy + Clone (line 117) - cheap to pass around\n\n---\n\n### 3. **cuda_memcpy Function**\n\n**Location:** `/home/georg/stark-backend/crates/cuda-common/src/copy.rs`, lines 42-59\n\n```rust\npub unsafe fn cuda_memcpy<const SRC_DEVICE: bool, const DST_DEVICE: bool>(\n    dst: *mut c_void,\n    src: *const c_void,\n    size_bytes: usize,\n) -> Result<(), MemCopyError>\n```\n\n**Key Details:**\n- **Generic const parameters** determine copy kind:\n  - `SRC_DEVICE=false, DST_DEVICE=false` → Host to Host\n  - `SRC_DEVICE=false, DST_DEVICE=true` → Host to Device\n  - `SRC_DEVICE=true, DST_DEVICE=false` → Device to Host\n  - `SRC_DEVICE=true, DST_DEVICE=true` → Device to Device\n- Wraps FFI binding `cudaMemcpyAsync` (line 29-35)\n- Uses per-thread stream: `cudaStreamPerThread`\n- Returns `Result<(), MemCopyError>`\n\n**FFI Binding:**\n```rust\n#[link(name = \"cudart\")]\nextern \"C\" {\n    fn cudaMemcpyAsync(\n        dst: *mut c_void,\n        src: *const c_void,\n        count: usize,\n        kind: cudaMemcpyKind,\n        stream: cudaStream_t,\n    ) -> i32;\n}\n```\n\n**Usage in codebase (example from data_transporter.rs, line 153):**\n```rust\nunsafe {\n    cuda_memcpy::<true, true>(\n        strided_trace.as_mut_raw_ptr(),\n        d_matrix_evals.as_raw_ptr(),\n        lifted_height * width * size_of::<F>(),\n    )?;\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n### 4. **transport_matrix_d2h_col_major Function**\n\n**Location:** `/home/georg/stark-backend/crates/cuda-backend/src/data_transporter.rs`, lines 307-312\n\n```rust\npub fn transport_matrix_d2h_col_major<T>(\n    matrix: &DeviceMatrix<T>,\n) -> Result<ColMajorMatrix<T>, MemCopyError> {\n    let values_host = matrix.buffer().to_host()?;\n    Ok(ColMajorMatrix::new(values_host, matrix.width()))\n}\n```\n\n**Used in `into_column_openings`:**\nLocation: `/home/georg/stark-backend/crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/mod.rs`\n\nThe function is called to transfer GPU-side DeviceMatrix to host ColMajorMatrix before splitting (example usage):\n```rust\nlet mat_host = transport_matrix_d2h_col_major(&mat)?;\nlet width = mat_host.width();\nlet height = mat_host.height();\ndebug_assert_eq!(height, 1, \"Matrices should have height=1 after folding\");\nlet air_width = if need_rot {\n    width / 2\n} else {\n    width\n};\n```\n\n---\n\n### Key Insights for Ownership and Views:\n\n1. **DeviceBuffer ownership:**\n   - Single owner (no Arc) - move semantics\n   - Create non-owning **views** via `view()` method → returns `DeviceBufferView`\n   - `DeviceBufferView` is `Copy` and holds raw pointer + size\n\n2. **DeviceMatrix s