: usize) -> Self` |\n| `as_view` | base.rs | 80 | `pub fn as_view(&self) -> DeviceMatrixView<'_, T>` |\n| `strong_count` | base.rs | 76 | `pub fn strong_count(&self) -> usize` (returns Arc ref count) |\n\n**Ownership Model:**\n- **Arc-wrapped buffer** - shared ownership via `Arc<DeviceBuffer<T>>`\n- Implements `Clone` (line 15) - cloning increments Arc ref count\n- Implements `Send + Sync` (unsafe impls at lines 12-13)\n- Has custom `Drop` impl (lines 25-33) that logs ref counts\n- **Use `as_view()` to create non-owning references** via `DeviceMatrixView<'a, T>` (lifetime-bounded view)\n\n**DeviceMatrixView (Non-owning View):**\n- Location: base.rs, lines 117-156\n- Uses `PhantomData<&'a T>` to enforce lifetime boundaries (line 122)\n- Unsafe constructor `from_raw_parts` (line 132): `pub unsafe fn from_raw_parts(ptr: *const T, height: usize, width: usize) -> Self`\n- Copy + Clone (line 117) - cheap to pass around\n\n---\n\n### 3. **cuda_memcpy Function**\n\n**Location:** `/home/georg/stark-backend/crates/cuda-common/src/copy.rs`, lines 42-59\n\n```rust\npub unsafe fn cuda_memcpy<const SRC_DEVICE: bool, const DST_DEVICE: bool>(\n    dst: *mut c_void,\n    src: *const c_void,\n    size_bytes: usize,\n) -> Result<(), MemCopyError>\n```\n\n**Key Details:**\n- **Generic const parameters** determine copy kind:\n  - `SRC_DEVICE=false, DST_DEVICE=false` → Host to Host\n  - `SRC_DEVICE=false, DST_DEVICE=true` → Host to Device\n  - `SRC_DEVICE=true, DST_DEVICE=false` → Device to Host\n  - `SRC_DEVICE=true, DST_DEVICE=true` → Device to Device\n- Wraps FFI binding `cudaMemcpyAsync` (line 29-35)\n- Uses per-thread stream: `cudaStreamPerThread`\n- Returns `Result<(), MemCopyError>`\n\n**FFI Binding:**\n```rust\n#[link(name = \"cudart\")]\nextern \"C\" {\n    fn cudaMemcpyAsync(\n        dst: *mut c_void,\n        src: *const c_void,\n        count: usize,\n        kind: cudaMemcpyKind,\n        stream: cudaStream_t,\n    ) -> i32;\n}\n```\n\n**Usage in codebase (example from data