{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_013hRPegBmJbBMoQu3gstWik","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Good, compiles. Now let me also reconsider the initial pack. The initial pack does ~2000 D2D copies to consolidate all mats into buf_a. But the benefit of having them contiguous is only for the FIRST fold round — subsequent rounds write output contiguously into the other buffer anyway.\n\nWhat if I skip the initial pack entirely and just allocate the ping-pong buffers? The first round would read from the original DeviceMatrix pointers (wherever they are), write output contiguously to buf_b. After swap, the foldable output is contiguous in buf_a. Non-foldable matrices keep their original DeviceMatrix objects.\n\nThis eliminates the initial pack overhead (~2ms D2D + freeing originals) while still getting the main benefit: no per-matrix allocation in the fold loop.\n\nLet me refactor the initialization to skip the D2D pack."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":225,"cache_read_input_tokens":133899,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":225},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d2c41f48-5b80-4de8-b307-355a7b8c0ec2","uuid":"31e24294-c200-4597-86a9-ef360726e5b8"}
